<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) & Prusinkiewicz et al. (2007) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation and accelerating plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 52.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py` (weighted score: 53.5/100). The Pass 1 baseline computes only a 1D quadratic polynomial for primordium count and a 2D single-order Vogel spiral without solving the coupled TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral gene-regulatory network ODEs, 3D multi-order recursive meristem trees across wild-type raceme, Arabidopsis ap1 cal, Brassica Cauliflower (beta=0), and Brassica Romanesco (beta>0) genotypes, 3D box-counting fractal dimension D_f, Fibonacci parastichy transitions (8,13) -> (13,21), lfy mutant negative controls, or computer-vision segmentation of the vendored Romanesco Brassica oleracea specimen. Overall 52.8/100 (faithfulness 49.8, reproducibility 59.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 53, Morphological realism / specimen match 45, Parameter expressivity 52, Morphometric validation 52, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 58, Reproducibility package 54. Output judged: docs/media/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py at 8871db0, image/png, 74902 B, 1300×585 px, artifact_sha256 f04c92d85381a93b4b5735b75000df6fc22c0142ec68d90b792975a1b86487ec (sha256 f04c92d85381a93b4b5735b75000df6fc22c0142ec68d90b792975a1b86487ec), spec_fingerprint 3b35051e2ba55236a89c013359c0e36df27af50f133cd223b665f430f960cce0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 3b35051e2ba55236a89c013359c0e36df27af50f133cd223b665f430f960cce0; artifact_sha256: f04c92d85381a93b4b5735b75000df6fc22c0142ec68d90b792975a1b86487ec; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/paper_citations.bib=4906c890ff71618e..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_reference.json=b580780d055808ce..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/romanesco_brassica_oleracea_specimen.jpg=5fba6c320b478d6c..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/scout_manifest.json=d684b2df5ef44398...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add runtime SHA-256 dataset verification, 9 reference-anchored morphometric measurements with statistical p-values and negative controls, and an 8-point deterministic `--self-test` suite.",
        "remediation needed: Implement automated computer-vision segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Romanesco Brassica oleracea specimen photograph (`romanesco_brassica_oleracea_specimen.jpg`) to extract the whole-curd conical aspect ratio, multi-scale secondary/tertiary floret cones, empirical self-similar scale ratio lambda, and 2D/3D fractal box-counting dimension.",
        "remediation needed: Implement the 3D multi-order recursive phyllotactic meristem tree solver across 4 hierarchical orders (n=4) and sweep plastochron acceleration beta in [0.0, 0.11], computing conical aspect ratio H/R, 3D box-counting fractal dimension D_f, and Voronoi/Delaunay Fibonacci contact parastichy pairs (8,13) -> (13,21).",
        "remediation needed: Implement the coupled TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 nonlinear Hill ODE gene-regulatory network solver (Azpeitia et al. 2021 Science; Prusinkiewicz et al. 2007 Science) across wild-type raceme (g_AP1=1), ap1 cal / curd mutants (g_AP1=0), and lfy loss-of-function negative control." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.28e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

